From a6dac7730ac3320cafb40ece49b24cb8427a710b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 13:17:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Driver Safety monitoring: harsh
 braking/acceleration/cornering, speeding
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New driving_events table (RLS: driver reads/writes own, owner reads for
their cars) + a weekly server-side-only Postgres function (pg_cron,
Mondays 03:00) that folds the past week's events into TrustScore — not
client-invocable, so a driver's device can never inflate its own score,
and the weighting is never exposed in the app.

Detection runs inside the existing background location pipeline (no
accelerometer/gyroscope access in a background task), purely from
consecutive GPS fixes:
- harsh braking/acceleration: change in GPS speed over elapsed time
- harsh cornering: change in GPS heading over elapsed time at speed
  (lateral accel = v * dHeading/dt), only evaluated above 20 km/h since
  heading is noisy at low speed
- speeding: a single explicit >120 km/h threshold — there's no
  per-road speed-limit data source wired up, so this is a deliberate,
  honest tradeoff (under-detects urban speeding) rather than guessing
  at a posted limit we don't have

Phone-usage-while-driving was dropped from scope per explicit decision:
it can't be reliably detected cross-platform without a manual
Android-only permission grant with no iOS equivalent.

New DrivingSafetyCard renders two variants from the same weekly
event counts: owner sees a blunt safety summary + overall assessment,
driver sees their score, a trend vs last week, and encouraging tips —
wired into the owner's driver detail screen and the driver's Activity
tab.
